---
import Layout from "../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Week1 from "../../../assets/weekOneSS.png";
import Week2 from "../../../assets/weekTwoPCBSS.png";
import Week3 from "../../../assets/weekThree.png";
import Week4 from "../../../assets/Counterboard.png";
import Week5 from "../../../assets/weekFive.png";
---

<Layout>
    <a href="/projects/" class="backToBtn">Back to Projects</a>

    <div class="projectPage">
        <h1>Resolution Hardware</h1><br /><br />
        <p>
            <em>Resolution Hardware</em> was an eight week program aimed at beginners
            to teach hardware. It was apart of a YSWS called <em>Resolution</em
            >, which had many pathways (hardware beuing one of them) that would
            be a crash course from zero to master. I only did hardware so I
            can't speak for the other pathways as they were all ran by different
            people but it seemed very unorganised at the time. I'll walk you
            through it week by week.
            <br>
            <br>
            <h2> Week One </h2>
            <img
            src={Week1.src}
            class="largeProjectImg"
            alt="My week one project.">
        </p>
    </div></Layout
>
